+`searchScriptItems()` finds text in the items `scriptItems()` gives, as the editor's search box does:
+in each item's name and command, a trigger's patterns, an alias's pattern, a script's event handlers,
+a button's commands and style sheet, and the Lua of all of them, the triggers first, then the aliases,
+scripts, buttons, timers and keys, as the editor lists its results. A name, a command and an alias's
+pattern give one match however often the text is in them; a pattern, an event handler and each line
+of a style sheet or of Lua give one for each place it is. Each match has its item's kind, id and name,
+the field it is in (`ScriptSearchField`), which pattern, event handler or line that is, from 0, the
+field or line itself and where the match starts in it. The text is found whatever its case unless
+asked otherwise, and with whole words only where it is a word of its own (`\b` before and after it,
+as the editor's option does). A frontend gives the most it will take, and is told when there were more.
+
